.TH "PCMSEND" "1" "October 23, 2026" "ka9q-radio" "ka9q-radio Manual"
.SH NAME
pcmsend \- send local audio as PCM over RTP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pcmsend
.RI "[options] -R destination"
.SH STATUS
.B Obsolete.
Use
.BR pcmrecord(1)
instead.
.SH DESCRIPTION
pcmsend captures two-channel audio at 48000 sample frames per second through
PortAudio and transmits RTP/UDP packets. It does not read an RTP input stream
or standard input. Audio is encoded as signed 16-bit big-endian PCM, normally
240 frames per packet (5 ms).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-I device"
Select capture device by exact PortAudio name or numeric index. Use -L to list
devices. An explicit input-capable device is recommended.
.TP
.B "\-R destination"
Set RTP destination. Required for normal operation; default port 5004.
.TP
.B "\-L"
List PortAudio devices and exit.
.TP
.B "\-T hops"
Set multicast TTL. Default 1.
.TP
.B "\-v"
Increase verbosity.
.TP
.B "\-V"
Print version and exit.
.SH LIMITATIONS
This is an older sender and does not generate the channel metadata used by
current ka9q-radio consumers. Verify compatibility with the intended receiver.
When no device is specified, the implementation currently selects the
PortAudio default output-device index even though it opens a capture stream;
choose a capture device explicitly.
.SH EXAMPLES
List devices and send from capture device 2:
.PP
.nf
pcmsend \-L
pcmsend \-I 2 \-R 239.1.2.3:5004
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
monitor(1), pcmrecord(1), radiod(8)
.PP
Project documentation: https://github.com/ka9q/ka9q-radio
